e the same agent, we can reference our own earlier statement as part of our own evidence? The instruction: \"Link evidence to candidates or alternatives.\" \"Distinguish your own information from information shared by others.\" So we should note which evidence came from our own data (original list) and which came from others (Agent 2, Agent 3). Our earlier public message is part of the discussion, but it's our own contribution. Might be considered \"shared by others\" now. But we can say \"my own data\" vs \"others' statements\". We'll do that.\n\nWe also need to note remaining uncertainty: communication difficulty, egocentric, low willingness for further education.\n\nWhat would change vote: evidence that another candidate's interpersonal weaknesses are not detrimental, or that C's communication issues are negligible.\n\nNow produce final output.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}\n\nProceed."}
